# doq: kept in English by the translator (name or code)
#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Inelastic neutron scattering and the dynamical structure factor {#inelastic-neutron-scattering-and-the-dynamical-structure-factor}"
msgstr "Inelastic neutron scattering and the dynamical structure factor {#inelastic-neutron-scattering-and-the-dynamical-structure-factor}"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Inelastic neutron scattering (INS) is one of the most powerful experimental probes of magnetic excitations in quantum materials. When a beam of thermal or cold neutrons impinges on a crystal, individual neutrons exchange both momentum $\\mathbf{q}$ and energy $\\omega$ with the magnetic subsystem. The measured scattering intensity is proportional to the dynamical structure factor (DSF),\n"
msgstr "Ang inelastic neutron scattering (INS) ay isa sa mga pinakamakapangyarihang experimental probe ng magnetic excitations sa quantum materials. Kapag tumama ang isang beam ng thermal o cold neutrons sa isang crystal, nagpapalitan ang mga indibidwal na neutron ng momentum $\\mathbf{q}$ at enerhiyang $\\omega$ kasama ang magnetic subsystem. Ang nasukat na scattering intensity ay proporsyonal sa dynamical structure factor (DSF),\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "$$S^{\\alpha\\beta}(q,\\omega) = \\sum_{j} e^{-iq\\,j}\\int_{-\\infty}^{\\infty} dt\\; e^{i\\omega t}\\, \\langle S_0^{\\alpha}(0)\\, S_j^{\\beta}(t)\\rangle,$$\n"
msgstr "$$S^{\\alpha\\beta}(q,\\omega) = \\sum_{j} e^{-iq\\,j}\\int_{-\\infty}^{\\infty} dt\\; e^{i\\omega t}\\, \\langle S_0^{\\alpha}(0)\\, S_j^{\\beta}(t)\\rangle,$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "which encodes the full space-time correlations of the spin degrees of freedom.\n"
msgstr "na naglalaman ng buong space-time correlations ng mga spin degrees of freedom.\n"

# doq: kept in English by the translator (name or code)
#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "KCuF$_3$: a canonical Luttinger-liquid magnet {#kcuf-3-a-canonical-luttinger-liquid-magnet}"
msgstr "KCuF$_3$: a canonical Luttinger-liquid magnet {#kcuf-3-a-canonical-luttinger-liquid-magnet}"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Potassium copper fluoride (KCuF$_3$) is a quasi-one-dimensional antiferromagnet in which chains of spin-$\\frac{1}{2}$ Cu$^{2+}$ ions interact via a nearest-neighbor Heisenberg exchange $J$, while the interchain coupling is only $\\sim 2.7\\%$ of $J$. At $T = 6\\;\\mathrm{K}$ where INS data are available, the spectrum is dominated by fractionalized spinon excitations characteristic of a Tomonaga-Luttinger liquid. Because the intrachain dynamics are well described by the one-dimensional spin-$\\frac{1}{2}$ XXZ Hamiltonian at the isotropic point ($\\epsilon = 1$),\n"
msgstr "Ang potassium copper fluoride (KCuF$_3$) ay isang quasi-one-dimensional antiferromagnet kung saan ang mga chain ng spin-$\\frac{1}{2}$ Cu$^{2+}$ ions ay nakikipag-interact sa pamamagitan ng nearest-neighbor Heisenberg exchange $J$, habang ang interchain coupling ay $\\sim 2.7\\%$ lamang ng $J$. Sa $T = 6\\;\\mathrm{K}$ kung saan available ang INS data, ang spectrum ay dominado ng fractionalized spinon excitations na katangian ng isang Tomonaga-Luttinger liquid. Dahil ang intrachain dynamics ay mahusay na inilalarawan ng one-dimensional spin-$\\frac{1}{2}$ XXZ Hamiltonian sa isotropic point ($\\epsilon = 1$),\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "$$H = J\\sum_{i}\\left[S_i^Z S_{i+1}^Z + \\epsilon\\left(S_i^X S_{i+1}^X + S_i^Y S_{i+1}^Y\\right)\\right],$$\n"
msgstr "$$H = J\\sum_{i}\\left[S_i^Z S_{i+1}^Z + \\epsilon\\left(S_i^X S_{i+1}^X + S_i^Y S_{i+1}^Y\\right)\\right],$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "KCuF$_3$ serves as an ideal benchmark for quantum simulation: the Hamiltonian is simple enough to implement on a quantum processor, yet the ground state is strongly entangled and the excitation spectrum features a broad two-spinon continuum.\n"
msgstr "Ang KCuF$_3$ ay nagsisilbing isang ideal na benchmark para sa quantum simulation: sapat na simple ang Hamiltonian upang maipatupad sa isang quantum processor, ngunit ang ground state ay lubos na entangled at ang excitation spectrum ay nagtataglay ng malawak na two-spinon continuum.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Note: this tutorial sets $J = 1$ as the energy unit and adopts the normalization $H = J\\sum_i[\\ldots]$, which corresponds to the local Hamiltonian $H_\\mathrm{loc} = J(S^X S^X + S^Y S^Y + S^Z S^Z)$ used in the paper's circuit implementation (Fig. S3 of the supplementary). The paper's full Hamiltonian (Eq. 3) carries an additional overall factor of 2, so the paper's $J$ is twice the $J$ used here.\n"
msgstr "Tandaan: itinatakda ng tutorial na ito ang $J = 1$ bilang unit ng enerhiya at ginagamit ang normalization na $H = J\\sum_i[\\ldots]$, na katumbas ng local Hamiltonian na $H_\\mathrm{loc} = J(S^X S^X + S^Y S^Y + S^Z S^Z)$ na ginamit sa circuit implementation ng papel (Fig. S3 ng supplementary). Ang buong Hamiltonian ng papel (Eq. 3) ay may karagdagang overall factor na 2, kaya ang $J$ ng papel ay doble ng $J$ na ginamit dito.\n"

# doq: kept in English by the translator (name or code)
#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "What we simulate and measure {#what-we-simulate-and-measure}"
msgstr "What we simulate and measure {#what-we-simulate-and-measure}"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The physical quantity we compute is the **retarded Green's function** (RGF), defined as the time-dependent spin-spin correlation function\n"
msgstr "Ang pisikal na dami na kinakalkula natin ay ang **retarded Green's function** (RGF), na tinukoy bilang ang time-dependent spin-spin correlation function\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "$$G^R_{\\alpha,\\beta}(j, j_c, t) = -\\frac{i}{2}\\,\\langle\\psi_{\\mathrm{GS}}|\\,S_j^\\alpha(t)\\,S_{j_c}^\\beta(0) - S_{j_c}^\\beta(0)\\,S_j^\\alpha(t)\\,|\\psi_{\\mathrm{GS}}\\rangle,$$\n"
msgstr "$$G^R_{\\alpha,\\beta}(j, j_c, t) = -\\frac{i}{2}\\,\\langle\\psi_{\\mathrm{GS}}|\\,S_j^\\alpha(t)\\,S_{j_c}^\\beta(0) - S_{j_c}^\\beta(0)\\,S_j^\\alpha(t)\\,|\\psi_{\\mathrm{GS}}\\rangle,$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "where $j_c$ is a reference site (the chain center) and $S_j^\\alpha(t) = e^{iHt}S_j^\\alpha e^{-iHt}$ is the Heisenberg-picture spin operator. In this tutorial we focus on the $zz$ component ($\\alpha = \\beta = z$). On a quantum computer the RGF is accessed by preparing the ground state, applying a local perturbation at $j_c$, time-evolving the perturbed state, and measuring the single-qubit expectation value $\\langle\\sigma_j^z\\rangle$ at every site $j$ for each time step. The key insight is that each $\\langle\\sigma_j^z\\rangle$ gives the difference from the ground-state magnetization; because the isotropic Heisenberg antiferromagnet has zero net per-site magnetization ($\\langle\\sigma_j^z\\rangle_\\mathrm{GS} = 0$), the raw measured value directly yields $G^R(j, j_c, t)$ without any explicit subtraction.\n"
msgstr "kung saan ang $j_c$ ay isang reference site (ang gitna ng chain) at ang $S_j^\\alpha(t) = e^{iHt}S_j^\\alpha e^{-iHt}$ ay ang Heisenberg-picture spin operator. Sa tutorial na ito, nakatuon tayo sa $zz$ component ($\\alpha = \\beta = z$). Sa isang quantum computer, naa-access ang RGF sa pamamagitan ng paghahanda ng ground state, paglalapat ng lokal na perturbation sa $j_c$, time-evolving ng na-perturb na state, at pagsukat ng single-qubit expectation value na $\\langle\\sigma_j^z\\rangle$ sa bawat site $j$ para sa bawat time step. Ang mahalagang insight ay ang bawat $\\langle\\sigma_j^z\\rangle$ ay nagbibigay ng pagkakaiba mula sa ground-state magnetization; dahil ang isotropic Heisenberg antiferromagnet ay may zero net per-site magnetization ($\\langle\\sigma_j^z\\rangle_\\mathrm{GS} = 0$), direktang nagbubunga ang hilaw na sinukat na halaga ng $G^R(j, j_c, t)$ nang walang anumang explicit na pagbabawas.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "By collecting $G^R(j, j_c, t)$ over all sites and time steps, we assemble a two-dimensional dataset that is then Fourier-transformed in both space and time to produce the **dynamical structure factor** $S(q,\\omega)$. The DSF is the quantity directly measured in an INS experiment: it tells us what magnetic excitations exist at each momentum $q$ and energy $\\omega$. For the isotropic Heisenberg chain the exact excitation spectrum is a **two-spinon continuum**, a broad band of scattering intensity whose shape serves as a stringent end-to-end benchmark for the quantum simulation: it validates the ground-state preparation, perturbation, Trotter time evolution, and measurement protocol all at once.\n"
msgstr "Sa pamamagitan ng pagkolekta ng $G^R(j, j_c, t)$ sa lahat ng sites at time steps, binubuo natin ang isang two-dimensional dataset na pagkatapos ay Fourier-transformed sa parehong espasyo at oras upang makabuo ng **dynamical structure factor** $S(q,\\omega)$. Ang DSF ang dami na direktang sinusukat sa isang INS experiment: sinasabi nito sa atin kung anong magnetic excitations ang umiiral sa bawat momentum $q$ at enerhiyang $\\omega$. Para sa isotropic Heisenberg chain, ang eksaktong excitation spectrum ay isang **two-spinon continuum**, isang malawak na band ng scattering intensity kung saan ang hugis nito ay nagsisilbing mahigpit na end-to-end benchmark para sa quantum simulation: pinapatunayan nito ang ground-state preparation, perturbation, Trotter time evolution, at measurement protocol nang sabay-sabay.\n"

# doq: kept in English by the translator (name or code)
#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Quantum-simulation workflow {#quantum-simulation-workflow}"
msgstr "Quantum-simulation workflow {#quantum-simulation-workflow}"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The workflow mirrors the physics of an INS event. We (1) prepare the many-body ground state $|\\psi_{\\mathrm{GS}}\\rangle$ on $n$ qubits, (2) apply a local spin-flip perturbation $U_{j_c} = \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}(I - i\\sigma^z_{j_c})$ at the chain center to mimic the neutron's spin transfer, (3) evolve under $H$ for discrete time steps using second-order Trotterization, and (4) measure $\\langle\\sigma_i^z\\rangle$ on every qubit at each step to obtain the RGF. A two-dimensional discrete Fourier transform then yields the DSF $S(q,\\omega)$.\n"
msgstr "Ginagaya ng workflow ang pisika ng isang INS event. Tayo ay (1) naghahanda ng many-body ground state $|\\psi_{\\mathrm{GS}}\\rangle$ sa $n$ qubits, (2) naglalapat ng lokal na spin-flip perturbation $U_{j_c} = \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}(I - i\\sigma^z_{j_c})$ sa gitna ng chain upang gayahin ang spin transfer ng neutron, (3) nag-eebolba sa ilalim ng $H$ para sa discrete time steps gamit ang second-order Trotterization, at (4) sinusukat ang $\\langle\\sigma_i^z\\rangle$ sa bawat qubit sa bawat step upang makuha ang RGF. Ang isang two-dimensional discrete Fourier transform ay nagbubunga pagkatapos ng DSF $S(q,\\omega)$.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The observable we measure at every time step is $\\sigma_i^z$ on each qubit $i$. In Qiskit this is represented as a list of `SparsePauliOp` operators: one single-qubit $Z$ embedded in the $n$-qubit identity string for each site. These observables are constructed once per problem instance during the problem-mapping step (Step 1) and reused for every circuit at that scale.\n"
msgstr "Ang observable na sinusukat natin sa bawat time step ay ang $\\sigma_i^z$ sa bawat qubit $i$. Sa Qiskit, ito ay kinakatawan bilang isang listahan ng `SparsePauliOp` operators: isang single-qubit $Z$ na naka-embed sa $n$-qubit identity string para sa bawat site. Ang mga observable na ito ay konstrukto nang isang beses lamang sa bawat problem instance sa panahon ng problem-mapping step (Step 1) at muling ginagamit para sa bawat circuit sa sukat na iyon.\n"

# doq: kept in English by the translator (name or code)
#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Approximate quantum compiling (AQC) {#approximate-quantum-compiling-aqc}"
msgstr "Approximate quantum compiling (AQC) {#approximate-quantum-compiling-aqc}"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Deep Trotter circuits can be compressed with **approximate quantum compiling (AQC)**, which replaces the first several Trotter layers with a shorter parameterized ansatz whose parameters are classically optimized to maximize the MPS-level fidelity with the original deep circuit. The remaining Trotter steps are appended exactly, producing a \"mixed\" AQC + Trotter circuit with substantially fewer two-qubit gates.\n"
msgstr "Ang malalalim na Trotter circuits ay maaaring i-compress gamit ang **approximate quantum compiling (AQC)**, na pinapalitan ang unang ilang Trotter layers ng isang mas maikling parameterized ansatz kung saan ang mga parameter nito ay classically optimized upang i-maximize ang MPS-level fidelity kasama ang orihinal na malalim na circuit. Ang natitirang mga Trotter step ay eksaktong idinaragdag, na gumagawa ng isang \"mixed\" AQC + Trotter circuit na may malaking bawas na two-qubit gates.\n"

# doq: kept in English by the translator (name or code)
#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "MPS simulation {#mps-simulation}"
msgstr "MPS simulation {#mps-simulation}"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "For a one-dimensional system, matrix-product-state (MPS) methods can efficiently simulate both ground-state preparation (with the density matrix renormalization group, or DMRG) and circuit-level time evolution. By controlling the bond dimension $\\chi$, we trade off accuracy against computational cost. In this tutorial we use MPS simulation within `qiskit-addon-aqc-tensor` to compute high-fidelity AQC ansätze that compress the deep Trotter circuits for hardware execution.\n"
msgstr "Para sa isang one-dimensional na sistema, ang matrix-product-state (MPS) methods ay mahusay na nakapag-simulate ng parehong ground-state preparation (gamit ang density matrix renormalization group, o DMRG) at circuit-level time evolution. Sa pamamagitan ng pagkontrol sa bond dimension $\\chi$, ipinagpapalit natin ang accuracy laban sa computational cost. Sa tutorial na ito, gumagamit tayo ng MPS simulation sa loob ng `qiskit-addon-aqc-tensor` upang kalkulahin ang high-fidelity AQC ansätze na nagko-compress ng malalalim na Trotter circuits para sa hardware execution.\n"

