# doq: kept in English by the translator (name or code)
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "Small-scale simulator example {#small-scale-simulator-example}"
msgstr "Small-scale simulator example {#small-scale-simulator-example}"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "We first demonstrate the full workflow on **10 qubits**, optimizing the HVA ground-state ansatz by using MPS simulation and using the Qiskit statevector simulator for time evolution. DMRG gives a reference ground-state energy and a reference MPS. This small-scale example lets us validate every step before scaling up.\n"
msgstr "Una nating ipinapakita ang buong workflow sa **10 qubits**, ino-optimize ang HVA ground-state ansatz gamit ang MPS simulation at ginagamit ang Qiskit statevector simulator para sa time evolution. Nagbibigay ang DMRG ng reference ground-state energy at isang reference MPS. Ang maliit na halimbawang ito ay nagbibigay-daan sa atin na patunayan ang bawat hakbang bago mag-scale up.\n"

# doq: kept in English by the translator (name or code)
#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Step 1: Map classical inputs to a quantum problem {#step-1-map-classical-inputs-to-a-quantum-problem}"
msgstr "Step 1: Map classical inputs to a quantum problem {#step-1-map-classical-inputs-to-a-quantum-problem}"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "We begin by defining the physical model and constructing the quantum circuits.\n"
msgstr "Nagsisimula tayo sa pagtukoy ng pisikal na modelo at pagbuo ng quantum circuits.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "**Hamiltonian.** KCuF$_3$ is modeled by the 1D XXZ Hamiltonian at the isotropic point ($J = 1$, $\\epsilon = 1$, setting $J = 1$ as the energy unit).\n"
msgstr "**Hamiltonian.** Ang KCuF$_3$ ay minomodelo ng 1D XXZ Hamiltonian sa isotropic point ($J = 1$, $\\epsilon = 1$, itinatakda ang $J = 1$ bilang unit ng enerhiya).\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "**Ground state.** We use a Hamiltonian variational ansatz (HVA) circuit, `build_ground_state_ansatz`, as the ground-state preparation circuit. The HVA parameters are optimized classically by maximizing the state fidelity $|\\langle\\psi_{\\mathrm{HVA}}(\\theta)|\\psi_{\\mathrm{DMRG}}\\rangle|^2$ with the DMRG ground-state MPS, where the HVA state is evaluated by simulating the circuit as a matrix product state with quimb's `CircuitMPS`. We use `scipy.optimize.minimize` for the optimization. The energy $\\langle H \\rangle$ of the optimized ansatz is also computed for reference.\n"
msgstr "**Ground state.** Gumagamit tayo ng isang Hamiltonian variational ansatz (HVA) circuit, `build_ground_state_ansatz`, bilang ground-state preparation circuit. Ang mga HVA parameter ay classically optimized sa pamamagitan ng pag-maximize ng state fidelity na $|\\langle\\psi_{\\mathrm{HVA}}(\\theta)|\\psi_{\\mathrm{DMRG}}\\rangle|^2$ kasama ang DMRG ground-state MPS, kung saan ang HVA state ay sinusuri sa pamamagitan ng pag-simulate ng circuit bilang matrix product state gamit ang `CircuitMPS` ng quimb. Ginagamit natin ang `scipy.optimize.minimize` para sa optimization. Ang enerhiyang $\\langle H \\rangle$ ng na-optimize na ansatz ay kinakalkula rin bilang reference.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "**Trotter gates.** Each nearest-neighbor interaction term $e^{-i\\Delta t\\, H_{\\mathrm{pair}}}$ with $H_{\\mathrm{pair}} = (J/4)(XX + YY + ZZ)$ is constructed with `PauliEvolutionGate(H_pair, time=time_step)`. Qiskit synthesizes this into the optimal three-CNOT decomposition during transpilation.\n"
msgstr "**Trotter gates.** Ang bawat nearest-neighbor interaction term na $e^{-i\\Delta t\\, H_{\\mathrm{pair}}}$ na may $H_{\\mathrm{pair}} = (J/4)(XX + YY + ZZ)$ ay binubuo gamit ang `PauliEvolutionGate(H_pair, time=time_step)`. Sini-synthesize ito ng Qiskit sa optimal na three-CNOT decomposition sa panahon ng transpilation.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "**Perturbation.** An $R_z(\\pi/2)$ gate on the center qubit implements $U_{j_c} = \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}(I - i\\sigma^z_{j_c})$, mimicking the local spin-flip produced by a scattered neutron.\n"
msgstr "**Perturbation.** Isang $R_z(\\pi/2)$ gate sa gitnang qubit ang nagpapatupad ng $U_{j_c} = \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}(I - i\\sigma^z_{j_c})$, ginagaya ang lokal na spin-flip na ginagawa ng isang scattered neutron.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "**Observables.** We construct a $\\sigma^z$ observable for each qubit site. These `SparsePauliOp` objects are passed to the Estimator primitive in Step 3 to extract $\\langle\\sigma_i^z\\rangle$ at every time step.\n"
msgstr "**Observables.** Bumubuo tayo ng $\\sigma^z$ observable para sa bawat qubit site. Ang mga `SparsePauliOp` object na ito ay ipinapasa sa Estimator primitive sa Step 3 upang makuha ang $\\langle\\sigma_i^z\\rangle$ sa bawat time step.\n"

# doq: kept in English by the translator (name or code)
#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Step 2: Optimize problem for quantum hardware execution {#step-2-optimize-problem-for-quantum-hardware-execution}"
msgstr "Step 2: Optimize problem for quantum hardware execution {#step-2-optimize-problem-for-quantum-hardware-execution}"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "For real hardware, the Trotter circuits above would be too deep. **Approximate quantum compiling (AQC)** addresses this by replacing the first $k$ Trotter layers (including the ground-state circuit) with a shorter parameterized ansatz optimized to maximize the MPS-level fidelity with the original deep circuit. The remaining Trotter steps are appended exactly, producing a shallower \"AQC + Trotter\" circuit.\n"
msgstr "Para sa aktwal na hardware, ang mga Trotter circuits sa itaas ay masyadong malalim. Ang **approximate quantum compiling (AQC)** ay tumutugon dito sa pamamagitan ng pagpalit sa unang $k$ Trotter layers (kasama ang ground-state circuit) ng isang mas maikling parameterized ansatz na na-optimize upang i-maximize ang MPS-level fidelity kasama ang orihinal na malalim na circuit. Ang natitirang mga Trotter step ay eksaktong idinaragdag, na gumagawa ng mas mababaw na \"AQC + Trotter\" circuit.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "To balance expressibility against circuit depth, two ansätze are used: a **one-layer ansatz** (generated from a single Trotter step) compresses the earliest time steps, and a deeper **two-layer ansatz** (generated from two Trotter steps) compresses the next few steps where higher fidelity is needed.\n"
msgstr "Upang balansehin ang expressibility laban sa lalim ng circuit, dalawang ansätze ang ginagamit: ang isang **one-layer ansatz** (nabuo mula sa isang Trotter step) ay nagko-compress ng pinakaunang time steps, at ang mas malalim na **two-layer ansatz** (nabuo mula sa dalawang Trotter step) ay nagko-compress ng susunod na ilang steps kung saan kailangan ang mas mataas na fidelity.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The AQC workflow has four sub-steps:\n"
msgstr "Ang AQC workflow ay may apat na sub-step:\n"

#. type: Bullet: '1. '
#, no-wrap
msgid "**Build target circuits** &mdash; the first $k_1 + k_2$ circuits from Step 1 serve directly as AQC targets.\n"
msgstr "**Bumuo ng target circuits** &mdash; ang unang $k_1 + k_2$ circuits mula sa Step 1 ay direktang nagsisilbing AQC targets.\n"

#. type: Bullet: '2. '
#, no-wrap
msgid "**Compute target MPS** &mdash; simulate each target circuit as a matrix-product state using `quimb.tensor.CircuitMPS`.\n"
msgstr "**Kalkulahin ang target MPS** &mdash; i-simulate ang bawat target circuit bilang matrix-product state gamit ang `quimb.tensor.CircuitMPS`.\n"

#. type: Bullet: '3. '
#, no-wrap
msgid "**Generate and optimize ansätze** &mdash; `generate_ansatz_from_circuit` creates a one-layer and a two-layer parameterized ansatz; parameters are optimized by using L-BFGS-B with JAX-accelerated gradients to minimize $1 - |\\langle\\psi_{\\mathrm{ansatz}}|\\psi_{\\mathrm{target}}\\rangle|^2$. The first $k_1$ steps use the one-layer ansatz and the next $k_2$ steps use the two-layer ansatz; within each stage, each step warm-starts from the previous step's optimized parameters, and parameters are reset to the stage defaults at the stage boundary.\n"
msgstr "**Bumuo at i-optimize ang mga ansätze** &mdash; gumagawa ang `generate_ansatz_from_circuit` ng isang one-layer at isang two-layer na parameterized ansatz; ang mga parameter ay na-optimize gamit ang L-BFGS-B na may JAX-accelerated gradients upang i-minimize ang $1 - |\\langle\\psi_{\\mathrm{ansatz}}|\\psi_{\\mathrm{target}}\\rangle|^2$. Ang unang $k_1$ steps ay gumagamit ng one-layer ansatz at ang susunod na $k_2$ steps ay gumagamit ng two-layer ansatz; sa loob ng bawat stage, ang bawat step ay warm-starts mula sa na-optimize na parameters ng naunang step, at ang mga parameter ay na-reset sa stage defaults sa hangganan ng stage.\n"

#. type: Bullet: '4. '
#, no-wrap
msgid "**Assemble mixed circuits** &mdash; for time steps beyond the AQC checkpoint, append exact Trotter layers to the optimized two-layer AQC circuit using `trotter_evolution`.\n"
msgstr "**Buuin ang mixed circuits** &mdash; para sa time steps lampas sa AQC checkpoint, idinaragdag ang eksaktong Trotter layers sa na-optimize na two-layer AQC circuit gamit ang `trotter_evolution`.\n"

