#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The hardware results reproduce the key features of the two-spinon continuum: the scattering intensity is concentrated near the antiferromagnetic wave vector $q = \\pi$ at low energy and is bounded from below by the sinusoidal spinon dispersion, with a broad continuum of spectral weight above it rather than a single sharp mode. This is the same structure measured by inelastic neutron scattering on KCuF$_3$, and it validates the full workflow of ground-state preparation, perturbation, AQC-compressed Trotter evolution, and error-mitigated measurement at the 50-qubit scale.\n"
msgstr "Ginagaya ng mga hardware result ang mga pangunahing katangian ng two-spinon continuum: ang scattering intensity ay nakakonsentra malapit sa antiferromagnetic wave vector na $q = \\pi$ sa mababang enerhiya at bounded mula sa ibaba ng sinusoidal spinon dispersion, na may malawak na continuum ng spectral weight sa itaas nito sa halip na iisang sharp mode. Ito ang parehong istraktura na nasukat ng inelastic neutron scattering sa KCuF$_3$, at pinapatunayan nito ang buong workflow ng ground-state preparation, perturbation, AQC-compressed Trotter evolution, at error-mitigated measurement sa sukat na 50-qubit.\n"

